      "problem": "$\\frac{4}{9}÷5=$",
      "worked_solution": "Dividing a fraction by a whole number is equivalent to multiplying the fraction by the reciprocal of that whole number.\n\nThe reciprocal of $5$ is $\\frac{1}{5}.$ So, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{4}{9}\\,÷\\,5=\\frac{4}{9}\\,\\times \\,\\frac{1}{5}.\n$$\n\n \n\nNow, we multiply fractions. We multiply the numerators, and we multiply the denominators:\n\n$$\n\\frac{4}{9}\\times \\frac{1}{5}=\\frac{4\\times 1}{9\\times 5}=\\frac{4}{45}\n$$",
